# Custom lib — app/src/lib/text.ts

## Context

`app/src/lib/text.ts` is a small in-house text helper library, not
lodash/underscore. Its entire supported surface is three functions.

## Rule

- The only functions that exist are:
  - `slugify(input: string): string`
  - `truncate(input: string, maxLength: number, suffix?: string): string`
  - `normalizeSpaces(input: string): string`
- Do NOT call or import helpers like `capitalize`, `camelCase`, `deburr`,
  `kebabCase`, `pad`, or any other lodash/underscore-style helper — they do
  not exist in this lib.
- If new text behavior is needed, add a new named export to
  `app/src/lib/text.ts` explicitly (with a colocated test in
  `app/src/lib/text.test.ts`) rather than assuming it already exists elsewhere.
- Do not import a general-purpose string utility package (e.g. lodash) as a
  substitute — extend the in-house lib instead.

## How to verify

1. `grep -n "^export function" app/src/lib/text.ts` — output is exactly
   `slugify`, `truncate`, `normalizeSpaces` (plus any function explicitly added
   in this session, each with a matching test).
2. `grep -rn "capitalize\|camelCase\|deburr\|kebabCase" app/src` — no matches
   unless just added as a real implementation.
3. `grep -n "lodash\|underscore" app/package.json app/src` — no matches.
4. `cd app && npm test -- text.test.ts` (or `npm test`) passes.
